---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Colophon — Mihnea Catana" description="How this site is made: typography, colors, and code.">
  <section class="section container">
    <h1 class="h-display h2 reveal page-title">
      <span class="reveal-inner">Colophon<em class="accent-word">.</em></span>
    </h1>

    <div class="prose prose--drop fade-up" style="--d: 1">
      <p>A colophon is a site telling you how it was made. This one believes in showing its work.</p>

      <h2>Typography</h2>
      <p>
        Headlines are set in <a href="https://github.com/joeprins/questrial" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Questrial</a>,
        body text in <a href="https://github.com/Instrument/instrument" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Instrument Sans</a>, and
        the small caps labels in <a href="https://www.ibm.com/plex/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IBM Plex Mono</a>. All fonts are
        self-hosted — no requests leave this site for a font file.
      </p>

      <h2>Colors</h2>
      <p>
        Sage paper <code>#F1F3EF</code>, green-black ink <code>#15201A</code>, and one deep viridian accent
        <code>#14513B</code> that has to earn its place. If a page needs more than one accent color, the
        design was wrong.
      </p>

      <h2>Under the hood</h2>
      <p>
        Built with <a href="https://astro.build" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Astro</a>, which ships
        this page as static HTML with a small sprinkle of vanilla JavaScript for the motion. No client-side
        framework, no trackers, no analytics — I have no idea how many people read this, and I've made peace
        with it.
      </p>

      <h2>Motion</h2>
      <p>
        Every animation respects <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>. If your OS asks for less motion, you'll
        get a perfectly still site that reads exactly the same.
      </p>

      <h2>One more thing</h2>
      <p>
        If you type <code>hello</code> anywhere on this site, something small says hi back. It does nothing
        useful, which is precisely the point.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-title {
    margin-bottom: clamp(2.2rem, 6vh, 3.5rem);
  }
</style>
